// Detection: Account Lockout Monitoring
// Focus: IT operations
// ATT&CK: T1110 (Brute Force), related only. A lockout alone is not evidence of an attack.
// Description: Lists account lockouts (event 4740) recorded on the domain controller,
// showing which account was locked and which machine the bad attempts came from.
// Notes:
//  - In a 4740 event, TargetDomainName holds the caller computer, not a domain.
//    It is renamed CallerComputer here so the output says what it means.
//  - Requires an account lockout threshold on the domain. The default is 0, which never locks.
//  - Sentinel displays time in UTC.

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4740
| project TimeGenerated, LockedAccount = TargetUserName, CallerComputer = TargetDomainName, DomainController = Computer
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
